<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Frederick of Waldeck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1620–1692</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Frederick of Waldeck was a German count and prince who served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> as a soldier and statesman. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> field marshal under William III he commanded allied armies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war">Nine Years' War</a>, losing at Fleurus in 1690. The Emperor raised him to the rank of prince in 1682.</p></div>
